Comment:
 This is the license of the Lawrence Berkeley Laboratory (LBL) code in
 tcpdump; "BSD-4-Clause-Shortened" is its SPDX identifier.
 .
 The University of California, Berkeley has deleted the advertising clause
 of its BSD license twice: on 22 July 1999 for "those BSD Unix files"
 containing the clause "This product includes software developed by the
 University of California, Berkeley and its contributors", and on 31
 January 2012 for "software officially licensed by UC Berkeley using the
 original 4-clause BSD license". Neither amendment clearly covers this
 license: its acknowledgement names Lawrence Berkeley Laboratory rather
 than "the University of California, Berkeley", and its text is not the
 numbered 4-clause BSD license that the amendments quote. Several files
 under it also have copyright holders other than the University of
 California. The advertising clause is therefore treated as still in
 effect.

